Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-24-2000||02:15 PM||||OK so just over a year ago I bought a 1992 Mustang GT Convert from CarMax. It was loaded. (Triple Black with leather) It had 47,000 miles on it. I went to the dealer to loOK for a car for my girlfriend, but when I saw it I thought ... Why don't get another toy for me (If the price is right). I asked the salesmen how much.. He said $11,000..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I expressed my disappointment in that price. The salesmen asked how much do you think its worth. I told him Ill give him $9000. He said no we don't negotiate the price. So I said OK no problem & left. 2 weeks later he called me & said they will sell me the car for $9500. That weekend I went and picked it up. Well just over 365 days later the car has been in for service on & off 92 days.Its had a long list of problems but the worst one is the rear axle. It's been in 5 times to rebuild & they never fixed it. After long shouting matches with the managers at the dealer I just called a lawyer. Well last week the lawyer called me and said CarMax will buy your car back and pay you for your trouble. WOO HOO!!! The lawyer told me that he has sued CarMax over 100 times & they never goto court. So now Im droping off the car and they will cut me a check on the spot next week.<P>Just to let you know. CarMax uses used parts to fix there cars. (example: I had a broken baffle in the gas tank. CarMax told me that they replaced it with a NEW one. The lawyer found out that it was a rusty used one from a bone yard.<P>If you have a CarMax car please look at it close when you get it back from service.<P><BR>Now Im going to get a 2001 Jeep Cherokee.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P> <BR> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||10
Z||000001||fropuff||11-24-2000||07:33 PM||||Nice job.  Nothing like driving a nice car without paying for it.  Good luck with the Cherokee.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||11-24-2000||10:35 PM||||Very similar situation happened with a coworker of mine.  She had to fight and fight with them to repair her car the right way in a reasonable amount of time, the first time.  Finally it came down to a lawyer sending a letter and they were very speedy after that and she has never had any problems with it since.<P>I would steer clear of Car Max in the future.  I knew a mechanic who worked there, and he said especially stay away from the "valueMax Deals" or the special deals they offer.  He said most of them will need major major work right about when the warranty runs out (they won't offer a long one).  <P>He gave me an example.  Trade in 1997 Neon.  Had a crack in the block, they used some type of sealant to repair that, then the tranny had been run with half the amount of fluid it was supposed to half for God knows how long (car had 60k miles).  They put it on the Value Max lot for %6,000 and it was sold in a week. They only gave the person 2,500 for the trade in due to these needed repairs so they more then doubled in profit and knowingly ripped someone off in the process....<P><BR> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
